=== 3. File Integrity Check ===
Command: printf "FIT4012 SHA file integrity sample\n" > sample.txt
Command: ./sha256 --hash-file sample.txt
Output : 5ee62dc925a9958dbd6732c570a23c7f65a8c11066e889b15068cfb4bf1a0bd9

Command: ./file_integrity sample.txt 5ee62dc925a9958dbd6732c570a23c7f65a8c11066e889b15068cfb4bf1a0bd9
Output :
[PASS] File integrity OK
SHA-256: 5ee62dc925a9958dbd6732c570a23c7f65a8c11066e889b15068cfb4bf1a0bd9

--- Tamper: append "tampered content" to file ---
Command: printf "tampered content\n" >> sample.txt
Command: ./file_integrity sample.txt 5ee62dc925a9958dbd6732c570a23c7f65a8c11066e889b15068cfb4bf1a0bd9
Output :
[FAIL] File was changed or expected hash is incorrect
expected: 5ee62dc925a9958dbd6732c570a23c7f65a8c11066e889b15068cfb4bf1a0bd9
actual  : a69e0b7a0768cf3c7258b5ee277b9238604a97be5cec4a6e79eafd5d94a065ba

[PASS] Tamper case correctly detected.

